  "answer_core": "You should not grant Marcus 15% equity, a board seat, and a CTO title this week. Those are too permanent for a relationship that has not yet been tested on the specific dependencies that actually matter to the company.\n\nInstead, Friday should be a direct and structured conversation where you make two things clear: you take the partnership seriously, and any path to major upside requires evidence. Define a short, time‑boxed sprint that tests whether he can deliver the core platform work, whether that work proves revenue‑relevant, whether team continuity strengthens rather than concentrates risk, whether knowledge transfer occurs, and whether his governance behavior fits what the company needs. Make explicit what successful completion of that sprint would unlock.\n\nThis avoids both extremes: locking in irreversible commitments too early, and giving a vague \"later\" that pushes him away. The message is that there may be a path to real leadership and meaningful ownership, but not before the company sees what the partnership actually does to its stability and trajectory.",
